    <content:encoded>[caption id="attachment_1546" align="aligncenter" width="640"]&lt;a href="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/img_3590.jpeg"&gt;&lt;img class="size-large wp-image-1546" alt="King of the Sky" src="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/img_3590.jpeg?w=640" width="640" height="864" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; King of the Sky[/caption]

Things just move way too fast. This is Abel Tazman Lehman, Adam's son. He's only two, but he already dwarfs a Kansan variant of the Beech D18. He is very into trucks, cars, tractors, airplanes, anything with a motor. He is sporting a shirt from a tiny, tiny town in Ontario and his trip to Canada this summer is going to be the highlight of his scant years. Nothing but boats to vroom-vroom and cousins to clamber around the rocks with.</content:encoded>
